# FSD

Canon: [fsd.how](https://fsd.how). Check: `pnpm lint:fsd` (steiger).

## Steiger exceptions

File-scoped `rules: 'off'` lives in `frontend/steiger.config.ts`. One consumer → move the slice to that consumer; do not silence. An `off` without a reason on that disable naming why the move is impossible is a review finding.

## Astro

- `src/pages` — file-based routing only (thin entry points).
- FSD pages layer → `src/_pages` (imports `@/_pages/*`).
- Do not put slices/segments in `src/pages`.
- New **section** lives under the view until a second page needs it. Rule: `page-sections.mdc`.

## Layers (top to bottom)

`app` → `_pages` → `widgets` → `features` → `entities` → `shared`

Imports only downward. Slice public API — `index.ts` (named exports, not `export *`).

Do not export what nothing outside the file imports. Helper type — no `export`, or inline. `export` only when there is an external import.

Exception: `RawProps as XRawProps` on the section / view public API — transformers import it; do not wait for the first caller.

```ts
// ❌ useless export — type lives only in this file
export type OptionResult = {
  id: string;
  votes: number;
  percent: number;
};

export type PollResult = {
  options: OptionResult[];
};

// ✅ inline if used once
export type PollResult = {
  options: { id: string; votes: number; percent: number }[];
};

// ✅ no export if needed locally twice
type OptionResult = { id: string; votes: number; percent: number };
```
